WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.322
This six-step workflow is the pattern I want you to reuse throughout the module.

00:00:05.322 --> 00:00:09.297
First, state the rule in plain language.

00:00:09.297 --> 00:00:15.877
Before writing SQL, you should be able to explain the requirement to another person.

00:00:15.877 --> 00:00:22.242
For example: select active patients who have explicitly consented and who have either Diabetes or Kidney

00:00:22.242 --> 00:00:26.602
Disease. Second, identify which fields can be missing.

00:00:26.602 --> 00:00:30.982
If consent can be NULL, decide whether NULL means no, unknown, or needs review.

00:00:30.982 --> 00:00:36.562
That decision should come from the business meaning, not from convenience.

00:00:36.562 --> 00:00:39.337
Third, group related conditions with parentheses.

00:00:39.337 --> 00:00:45.772
This is especially important when AND and OR appear together.

00:00:45.772 --> 00:00:51.907
Parentheses make your intention visible and reduce the chance that operator precedence changes the meaning.

00:00:51.907 --> 00:00:59.277
Fourth, if you are using CASE, place the most specific or highest-priority branches first.

00:00:59.277 --> 00:01:02.007
Remember that CASE stops at the first true branch.

00:01:02.007 --> 00:01:08.387
Fifth, test edge cases. Try exact threshold values, such as exactly sixty-five years old.

00:01:08.387 --> 00:01:13.957
Test zero. Test NULL. Test empty text and text that contains only spaces.

00:01:13.957 --> 00:01:17.557
Test a row that satisfies more than one condition.

00:01:17.557 --> 00:01:21.157
Finally, compare the output with the written rule.

00:01:21.157 --> 00:01:27.237
Do not stop at “the query ran.” Ask whether every important row behaves as expected.

00:01:27.237 --> 00:01:30.677
You can use this workflow outside SQL too.

00:01:30.677 --> 00:01:37.427
It is essentially a small decision-modeling process: define the policy, identify uncertainty,

00:01:37.427 --> 00:01:41.679
encode the logic, test the boundaries, and validate the result.
